{"name":"Firebird Tail Lights","hex":"#dd5522","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"firebird","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A scarlet tanager (Piranga olivacea). (This species is now classified as belonging to the cardinal family: Cardinalidae)","A Baltimore oriole (Icterus galbula)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/firebird"},{"term":"tail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The caudal appendage of an animal that is attached to their posterior and near the anus or cloaca.","An object or part of an object resembling a tail in shape, such as the thongs on a cat-o'-nine-tails; a strand of material hanging from something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hold by the end; said of a timber when it rests upon a wall or other support; with in or into","To swing with the stern in a certain direction; said of a vessel at anchor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tail"},{"term":"lights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of light"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The lungs, now chiefly of an animal (being lighter than adjacent parts)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lights"}],"entries":[{"title":"Firebird (Slavic folklore)","blocks":[{"text":"In Slavic mythology and folklore, the firebird is a magical and prophetic glowing or burning bird from a faraway land which is both a blessing and a harbinger of doom to its captor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Firebird.jpg/330px-Firebird.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firebird_(Slavic_folklore)"},{"title":"Automotive lighting","blocks":[{"text":"Automotive lighting is functional exterior lighting in vehicles. A motor vehicle has lighting and signaling devices mounted to or integrated into its front, rear, sides, and, in some cases, top. Various devices have the dual function of illuminating the road ahead for the driver, and making the vehicle visible to others, with indications to them of turning, slowing or stopping, etc., with lights also indicating the size of some large vehicles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Reisebus.Heck.jpg/330px-Reisebus.Heck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automotive_lighting"},{"title":"Tail","blocks":[{"text":"The tail is the elongated section at the rear end of a bilaterian animal's body; in general, the term refers to a distinct, flexible appendage extending backwards from the midline of the torso. In vertebrate animals that evolved to lose their tails, the coccyx is the homologous vestigial of the tail. While tails are primarily considered a feature of vertebrates, some invertebrates such as scorpions and springtails, as well as snails and slugs, have tail-like appendages that are also referred to as tails."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg/330px-White-tailed_deer%2C_tail_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/PiouPiou87.jpg/500px-PiouPiou87.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/PiouPiou87.jpg/500px-PiouPiou87.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male golden pheasant at the Bloedel Floral Conservatory, Vancouver.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APiouPiou87.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Vasnetsov_samolet.jpg/500px-Vasnetsov_samolet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Vasnetsov_samolet.jpg/128